{#
  THE PRIVACY POLICY. Rewritten 2026-08-18, replacing the Termly-generated text
  transcribed from the previous site on 2026-08-01.

  WHY IT WAS REPLACED. The migrated version described a different business. It
  had sections on Financial Data and payment processors, shipping addresses,
  mobile applications, online chat, contests and giveaways, third-party
  advertisers, and interest-based advertising. None of it happens here.

  THE PARAGRAPH THAT MATTERED MOST WAS THE ANALYTICS ONE. It named Clicktale,
  Clicky, Crazy Egg, Google Analytics and Kissmetrics as vendors, and told the
  reader that by using the site they consented to collection by all of them.
  This build loads no analytics of any kind. Verified against the built output:
  the only scripts anywhere in _site are one JSON-LD block and the site's own
  module bundle. So the policy was obtaining consent for tracking that does not
  exist, which is a worse defect than an out-of-date policy. It is the kind of
  claim that is only ever found by reading the build rather than the document.

  The migrated-content banner is gone with it, for the same reason as on the
  accessibility statement: it stops being true once the text is ours.

  ============================================================
  EVERYTHING BELOW WAS ESTABLISHED BY READING THE BUILD. 2026-08-18.
  ============================================================

    no analytics        only two <script> tags exist across the whole of _site,
                        one JSON-LD and one first-party module
    no cookies          nothing sets document.cookie anywhere in src/js/
    no storage          no localStorage, sessionStorage or indexedDB
    fonts               fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com, per
                        src/_data/siteStats.json, for Lora only. Dual is
                        already self-hosted
    images              cdn.circulationstudio.com, 46 references in built HTML
    form                functions/api/contact.js, Cloudflare KV plus Resend
    retention           RETENTION_SECONDS in that Function, 730 days

  THE RETENTION NUMBER IS READ OFF THE MECHANISM, NOT CHOSEN HERE. The Function
  sets a 730 day KV expirationTtl and that is what deletes a submission. If that
  constant changes, this text is wrong the same day, which is why both carry a
  note pointing at the other.

  Cloudflare documents a 60 second minimum for expirationTtl and no maximum, so
  730 days is not near a cap. Confirmed against the documentation rather than
  against a live write, which needs credentials this repo does not hold.

  SCOPED, BECAUSE ONLY ONE HALF IS ENFORCED. The 24 months governs the form
  store. The delivered email sits in a mailbox and nothing in this system
  governs that, so no period is claimed for it. A retention period nothing
  enforces is a promise that is false the first time somebody checks.

  GOOGLE FONTS IS NAMED BECAUSE IT IS ACCURATE TODAY. Lora is served by Google
  Fonts and it is the only request that leaves our own infrastructure for a
  visitor who never submits the form. Lora is being self-hosted in a commit
  after the launch blockers, and .claude/CLAUDE.md carries the instruction to
  remove this disclosure in the same commit, so it cannot outlive its
  dependency.
#}

{% call container(class="cs-doc") %}
  <h1 class="cs-doc__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="cs-doc__date">Last updated {{ reviewed | calendarDate }}</p>

  <p class="cs-doc__lede">
    This site collects two things: what you type into the contact form, and the
    ordinary server records any website keeps. There is no analytics, there are
    no cookies, and nothing here tracks you between visits or between sites.
  </p>

  <div class="cs-doc__body">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>

    <h3>The contact form</h3>
    <p>If you write to us through the form, we receive your name, your email address, the message you write, and the website or listing address if you choose to give one. That last field is optional and the form says so.</p>
    <p>We also record the time of the submission and the IP address it came from. The IP is used to limit how many messages a single source can send in an hour, which is how the form resists automated abuse without a third-party spam service.</p>

    <h3>Server records</h3>
    <p>Our host records the requests it serves, which includes your IP address, the page requested, the time, and your browser's user agent string. This happens for every website you visit and is how a server is operated and secured. We do not combine these records with anything else or use them to build a profile.</p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <p>No analytics of any kind. No Google Analytics, no first-party analytics, no heatmaps, no session recording. We do not know how many people read a given page.</p>
    <p>No cookies. No tracking pixels. Nothing is written to your browser's local storage. No advertising networks and no interest-based advertising. We do not sell or share personal information, and we never have.</p>

    <h2>Who receives it</h2>
    <p>Four companies are involved in serving this site or handling a message you send. None of them receives anything for their own purposes.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and stores contact form submissions until they are deleted on the schedule below.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers your message to our inbox as an email.</li>
      <li><strong>Bunny CDN</strong> serves the photographs, so it receives the request for each image.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves one typeface used on this site, which means your browser requests a font file from Google and Google sees your IP address in doing so. This is the only request that leaves our own infrastructure for a visitor who never uses the form. We are moving that typeface onto our own server, and this line comes out when we do.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will also disclose information where the law requires it, or where we need to in order to establish or defend a legal claim. Nothing else.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>A contact form submission is deleted from our store 24 months after you send it. That is enforced automatically by an expiry set on the record when it is written, not by anyone remembering to do it.</p>
    <p>The email itself is a separate thing. Once your message reaches our inbox it becomes ordinary business correspondence and is kept with our other business records. We do not state a fixed period for the inbox, because nothing automatically enforces one and we would rather tell you that than claim a number.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to the address at the bottom of this page and we will respond within thirty days.</p>
    <p>California residents have these rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the CPRA, along with the right not to be treated differently for exercising them. Two of the rights that Act provides do not apply to us in practice: we do not sell personal information and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising, so there is nothing to opt out of. The categories we collect are identifiers, meaning your name, email address and IP address, and the contents of the message you choose to send.</p>
    <p>We do not respond to Do Not Track browser signals, because we do not track you whether the signal is set or not.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is for businesses and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect anything from a child. If you believe a child has sent us something, write to us and we will delete it.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>The site is served over HTTPS. Contact form submissions are stored on Cloudflare's network and are accessible only to us. No system is perfectly secure, and we are not going to claim otherwise, so please do not send anything sensitive through a web form. If you need to send us something confidential, call us and we will arrange a better route.</p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>Some pages link out to other websites, including Yelp, and one article links to a scheduling service where you can book a call with us. Following any of those links takes you somewhere with its own privacy practices, which we do not control. This policy covers only what happens on this site.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it. We do not consider your continued use of the site to be agreement to a new version, so if a change ever affects information you have already sent us, we will contact you rather than rely on you noticing this page.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For anything on this page, including a request to see or delete what we hold:</p>
    <p class="cs-doc__contact">
      {{ site.nap.name }}<br>
      {{ site.nap.streetAddress }}<br>
